{"author":"schacon+claude-opus@gmail.com","body":"150e18346; 17/17 passing. Two root causes: (1) push --receive-pack was a stub that ran the native in-process path then bailed 'failed to push some refs', so all 6 push subtests exited non-zero and no server-side trace2 ran — now an explicit non-default --receive-pack local push delegates to the working send-pack (spawns receive-pack -> server emits client-sid, client emits server-sid); (2) v2 fetch client sent session-id= AFTER the 0001 delim (as a fetch arg) so serve_v2 rejected it ('unexpected line') and the fetch aborted — moved it before the delim into the capability list (serve.c treats session-id as a .receive capability), fixing fetch v2 subtests 15 & 17."}